/**
 * @page topic_client_capture Media Capture
 * @ingroup module_client
 * @brief Capture, encode, and publish client video frames.
 *
 * Capture is a producer in the session pipeline. It obtains frames from the
 * configured media input, applies the active image/codec path, and sends through
 * the client connection's ACIP transport. It does not own a socket or framing
 * loop.
 *
 * @section client_capture_sources Sources
 *
 * Inputs may be webcams, files, network media, test patterns, or other FFmpeg
 * sources selected by the options layer. Capability probing and negotiated
 * dimensions/FPS belong to the media input and encoder; capture code must not
 * assume a camera exists.
 *
 * @section client_capture_send Sending
 *
 * Encoded video is handed to the transport through ACIP client send helpers.
 * The shared scheduler applies bounded admission and can drop disposable visual
 * media under pressure while preserving control traffic. Producers must honor
 * returned errors and stop cleanly during shutdown.
 *
 * @section client_capture_modes Modes
 *
 * Snapshot and test-pattern modes support automation and systems without camera
 * hardware. Recording occurs in the media pipeline before terminal presentation
 * and is independent of TUI visibility.
 *
 * @see topic_client_connection
 * @see topic_av
 * @see src/client/capture.c
 */
